WEBVTT

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:10.160
My lords, gentlemen,

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.840
pray silence for

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.580
Ralph Douglas Christopher

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.140
Alexander Gurney,

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.110
the 13th Earl of Gurney.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:28.840
The duty of the Society of St. George

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:30.000
is to keep

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:40.040
green the memory of England. We were once the rulers of the greatest empire the world

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:50.050
has ever known. Ruled not by superior force or skill, but by sheer presence.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:02:00.000
I give you, England, this teeming womb of privilege.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:10.320
this feudal state whose shores beat back the turbulent sea of foreign anarchy, this ancient

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:20.590
fortress still commanded by the noblest of our royal blood, this ancient land of ritual,

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:30.000
this precious stone set in the silver sea, the toast is England, this precious stone set

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.510
in the Silver Sea.

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:57.590
- Hear our speech, m'lord. - Well, Tuck, Englishmen like to hear the truth about themselves.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:58.680
He's back, Clare.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:04.430
Clare! I said Ralph is back.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.400
Thank you, Charles. I'll have a vodka and tonic.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.680
I say, Governor, the Governor's back.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.850
Mummy, I was just telling the Governor that the Governor's back.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.950
Charles! With ice!

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:22.070
I'm repeating myself, calling the Governor the Governor and Daddy the Governor as well.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.270
Suck, I'm getting married again. Very good, my lord.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.000
Miss Grace Sherry. Charles is right. Been putting it off for the sake of the family.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:41.570
only Jack left. This house used to be full of mischief. Four young devils. Thought I was

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:49.480
safe enough. Master Paul would have been the 14th Earl. District officer, 21. Dead, 23.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:05:00.000
Berry Berry. Picked it up off some scruffy fuzzy wuzzy in dressing gown. Master Richard used to play the

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.050
and young Raymond killed in Malaya.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:06.440
Not one of them buried in England.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.710
Never seen their graves.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.920
You could do that on a horrible, m'lord.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:18.720
Who's still, Jack?

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:29.410
Based on land.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:34.430
Can't have those knaves from Whitehall moving in, sir.

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:38.660
It's Miss Grace Shelley.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.650
- Is she any one, my lord? - No one.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:48.530
Charles recommends her. It's a good breeding stock, family foals well, sires mostly.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:52.770
There's always room at the top for brains, money, a good pair of titties.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:57.680
Miss Shelley seems well endowed, my lord.

00:06:01.470 --> 00:06:06.690
The Governor loved this bed. Took it all over the world with him.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:11.720
Devilish great man, Governor. Superb shot.

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.920
He did wonderful needlework, too.

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.160
What have you got there?

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:32.470
- Might I suggest the silk tonight, sir?

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.780
- Good idea, Tuck.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:41.160
For St. George, eh?

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:45.160
Ah, Tuck, there's no end to duty.

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:48.450
The law's been my life, Tuck.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.930
The judge can't be unreasonable.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.440
So how can he be a lover?

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:58.410
He parted a damn dry world, Tuck.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.570
- A long life.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:04.440
- And a grey one, my lord. - The power of life and death.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:08.260
The judge has no need for other vices.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:13.220
Once you put on the black cap, everything else tastes like wax fruit.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.910
Noose a bit high, Tuck. Bring it down half an inch.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:21.070
- That's it. - Will that be all, my lord?

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:24.390
Whiskey and soda in about five minutes, is it all?

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:26.980
Oh, Tuck, I shan't be dining tonight.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.000
Tell cook the trial ends tomorrow.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:33.460
So I shall be wanting one of her extra-large breakfasts in the morning.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.840
She knows I don't like passing sentence on an empty stomach.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:44.180
- Very good, my lord. - Thank you, Doug.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:51.050
Like a good English breakfast.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.730
Big meal of the day for the governor.

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.340
Always read the times through first,

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:59.640
in case there was anything too disturbing in it.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:06.330
Mother never knew what the word 'socialist' meant till she was past 50.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:14.720
Remember, standing at the foot of the bed there, telling him I wanted to be a painter.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:21.080
The Gurneys have never been slack, as he said. Earn their privileges.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.480
Great concession, letting me study law.

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.720
Not the Gurney tradition, though. Always the army.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:30.000
Feet! Feet! Feet!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.450
The boys are marching!

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.450
A little more grapes are Captain Bragg.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.360
Give 'em a touch of that cold steel, boys!

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:20.870
"Close, getting close. I can feel a hard breath. Wonderful, wonderful. One slip, wonderful.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:26.560
The worms have the best of it. They dine off the tenderest joints, juicy breasts, white thighs.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:36.280
'Tis a far, far better thing I do now than I've ever done.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:52.370
No, sir, no bandage.

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:57.270
I, my dear doctor, that is the last thing I shall do.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:11.720
Is that you, my love? Come to me. Come!

00:10:30.090 --> 00:10:34.070
Alexander, covered with honey and beeswax in his tomb,

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:37.920
felt the flowers growing over me.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.260
Oh, a man must have vision!

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:45.940
How else could an English judge and peer of the realm

00:10:46.020 --> 00:10:49.900
take moonlit trips to Marrakesh and Ponder's End?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.140
See six vestal virgins smoking cigars,

00:10:54.220 --> 00:11:00.000
Moses in bedroom slippers, naked bosoms floating past Formosa.

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:08.120
It's just time to be of good cheer, Master Ridley.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.450
Play the man.

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:13.230
There's plenty of time to win this game

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.900
and beat the Spaniards too.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:18.080
Form squirrels, men.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:22.210
Smash the Mahdi and bitty pounds, ah!

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:24.710
Ah, ah, ah!

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.620
Redego, Lordship.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:40.650
resurrection and life, saith the Lord. He that believeth in me, though he were dead,

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:52.560
yet shall he live. And whosoever liveth and believeth in me shall never die. Gilead is

00:12:52.560 --> 00:13:00.000
mine, and Manasseh is mine. Ephraim also is the strength of my head.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:06.700
Judah is my lawgiver, Moab is my washpot.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:15.010
Over Edom will I cast out my shoe, and upon Philistia will I triumph.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:25.670
Who will lead me into the strong city, and who will bring me into Edom?

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:04.890
An excellent service, Bertie. Created exactly the right impression.

00:14:04.930 --> 00:14:06.930
Dan, if I could understand a word of it.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:09.610
I hardly expected you to, my boy.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.450
Charles, I must have a word with you.

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:15.010
Charles, you see, this was a service which I could not have conducted

00:14:15.050 --> 00:14:19.290
for someone who may have laid thy violent hands upon himself.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.690
I wait a minute, Charles. A disturbing rumour has reached me.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:25.650
Now, tell me, did Ralph commit suicide?

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:26.880
Suicide?

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:30.000
Tucker found Ralph hanging in his bedroom wearing a cocked hat underpants.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.660
hands in a ballyskirt. Does that sound like suicide?

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.600
What? No. No, he does not.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:41.420
No, but I had to be sure, Charles. After all, he, well, he is buried in consecrated ground.

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:46.800
I must say, you know, it's damned odd to find Uncle Ralph hanging around like that in a ballyskirt.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:50.960
Charles, didn't you say Ralph was always rather, uh, artistic?

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:55.760
He was willful, stubborn, and this time he went too far, but he was my brother.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:15:00.000
Well, half-brother. I will not have you calling him artistic.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:05.510
- A cocked hat? - Tat? You said cocked hat, Charles. Why was Ralph wearing a cocked hat?

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:10.260
- Well, trying it on for size, obviously. I told him not to remain a widower.

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:14.280
The governor didn't. Had to start breeding again. Of course, not pleasant for a man Ralph's age,

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.130
but that was something he had to get on top of.

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:25.540
- Underpants? Why was... Why was he... Why was he in his underpants, Charles?

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:30.000
- Well, he was in his bedroom, wasn't he? I thought all our troubles would be over when he took effect.

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.180
That would have solved everything.

00:15:32.180 --> 00:15:34.160
Yes, wouldn't it just?

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:37.160
I do not know what all the bother is about.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:41.160
Uncle Ralph has got an heir. Jack, the 14th Earl.

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.140
Yes, there's always Jack.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:46.750
Yes, it's going to be awkward. Damned awkward.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:49.990
Well, Ralph knew the situation. I'm sure he's made proper arrangements.

00:15:49.990 --> 00:15:53.990
It's simply a matter of finding out who he's made legal guardian over the estate.

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:56.120
Belly-skirt?

00:15:56.120 --> 00:16:00.000
What on earth was he doing in a belly-skirt?

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:04.140
Holy scourth, Charles. Answer me that.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:06.670
Mr. Matthew Peake, to see you, Sir Charles.

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.560
Thank you, Tucker.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:11.380
Come on in, Peake.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.920
I think you know the one here.

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:14.900
I have that honour, Sir Charles.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:17.290
All right, that's all, Tucker. We're not to be disturbed.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:23.390
Might I suggest, Sir Charles, that Tucker stays?

00:16:23.390 --> 00:16:25.300
Hmm, quiet.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.000
Well, Tucker, it seems you're going to hear something to your advantage.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:28.810
Yes.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.000
You sit down, Tucker.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.880
May I take this opportunity to express my condolences?

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.160
Yes, yes, but do get on with it.

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:38.810
But, Sir Charles, shouldn't we wait?

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.660
I mean his lordship's heir.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:43.140
He's been notified, wasn't able to get away for the funeral,

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:44.630
so he's not likely to come now.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:49.820
I will inform you later.

00:16:49.820 --> 00:17:00.000
Ralph Douglas, Christopher Alexander,

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.640
Alexander Gurney of Gurney House and the County of Bedfordshire, hereby revoke all former

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:08.260
wills and connoisseurs and declare this to be my last will. I appoint Mr. Matthew Peake

00:17:08.260 --> 00:17:14.840
of 17 Brownlow Gardens Bedfordshire to be the sole executor of my will. I give and bequeath

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:20.260
unto my manservant Daniel Tucker the sum of £30,000 free of duty.

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:22.350
£30,000?

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:30.000
There follow a number of requests to various charities. I'll run through them briefly. I bequeath the sum of

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.710
5,000 pounds to the tail waivers registered national charity

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.840
3,000 pounds to the bankers beneficent society limited

00:17:41.120 --> 00:18:00.000
Cussing's a bit head on you

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.400
So are the ways of every one, my boy, who is greedy of gain.

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:06.500
Now then, people, what about the Zambezi mission?

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.000
And what about the overseas bishopric funds?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.500
Oh, never mind about them, Bertie.

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.420
- Charles, is that... - What about the estate?

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:16.840
I devise and bequeath the remainder of my estate,

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:19.440
both real and personal, whatsoever and wheresoever,

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:20.740
to which I might be entitled,

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:23.460
or over which I have any disposing at the time of my death,

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:30.000
to my beloved son, Jack Arnold Alexander Tancred Gurney, the...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:34.120
the 14th Earl of Gurney, for his own use, absolutely.

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:36.120
For his own use, absolutely?

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.710
Well, who's been appointed legal guardian?

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:40.490
No one.

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:44.600
By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:45.600
Yea, we wept.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.600
You mean Jack's free to run the estate and everything?

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.580
Jack will cheer up the House of Lords.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:54.630
Oh, Ralph obviously let his personal feelings come before his duty to his family.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:57.090
We've always left to fight. Awkward.

00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:00.000
There's bound to be a scandal, but there's no choice.

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:07.340
If this will be contested in any way, the whole of my estate, both real and personal, is bequeathed to the charities herewith.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:11.160
- The Earl Hague Father... - It's disgraceful!

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:15.300
- May God forgive him! - Bizarre! What a carved sense of humour!

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:19.300
- Father, I don't understand! - You ask him to explain before he explodes!

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:23.300
- Blast you! There's land at stake here! Darn it! - I'm completely in the fog!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.080
- When were you? - I don't understand what...

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:41.270
Ladies and gentlemen, the Queen's right trusty and well-beloved cousin Jack Arnold Alexander Tancred Gurney, 14th Earl of Gurney.

00:20:12.120 --> 00:20:12.620
Hello.

00:20:16.620 --> 00:20:18.120
I'm sorry I wasn't here before.

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:20.850
I received the news only yesterday.

00:20:20.850 --> 00:20:23.350
I'm afraid our little community is somewhat cut off.

00:20:23.350 --> 00:20:24.350
I hope he'll forgive me.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:25.890
I know he will.

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:27.910
I've just been to his grave.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.400
Thank you, Uncle Charles, for making all the arrangements.

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.780
Aunt Claire, you haven't changed.

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:39.470
No, you.

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:42.160
You must be Dinsdale.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:44.560
Yes, I suppose I must be. How do you do?

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.080
Are you still angry with me, Bishop?

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:55.700
Let me put your minds at rest.

00:20:56.680 --> 00:20:59.890
I'm coming back to take my place in the world.

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:09.030
The monastic ideal isn't easy. I've had many broken nights, but I'm coming back refreshed, though hardly equipped for society.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:17.060
I shall need your help, Charles. Come. We're all one family. Let's wash away the old sores.

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:19.960
If the bishop doesn't mind, I think we should pray.

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:26.940
Pray for love and understanding. Surely you pray for love and understanding.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.730
Every night, without success,

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:36.370
- You too, my son. - I'm a Methodist.

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:43.860
- I'm sure you're still a Christian. - Yes, my lord.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:11.520
prayer should rise up like incense prayer is an act of faith and union pray means to ask to beg

00:22:11.520 --> 00:22:18.420
to plead the prayer is a message to heaven you're talking directly to god express your desires freely

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:30.000
don't be afraid i know them already i am the creator and ruler of the universe koda the one supreme

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:39.050
Being an infinite personal being Yahwah, Shangri, T and El, the first immovable mover, yay!

00:22:39.050 --> 00:22:58.550
Salute!

00:22:58.550 --> 00:23:00.000
His lordship is a paranormal.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.240
Paranoid, schizophrenic?

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:04.360
Paranoid, schizophrenic?

00:23:04.360 --> 00:23:05.360
But he's a gurney.

00:23:05.360 --> 00:23:09.470
Then he's a paranoid, schizophrenic gurney who believes he's God.

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:11.520
But we've always been Church of England.

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:17.060
His idea of the world we live in is determined solely by his feelings.

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:19.010
What he feels is, is.

00:23:19.010 --> 00:23:22.980
If my nephew is bonkers, why the blazes would you let him out?

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:27.080
He's a voluntary patient in a private clinic, free to go whenever he chooses.

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:29.890
His father insisted on no official certification.

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:33.980
If you want him detained here permanently, you must bring him before the board of control

00:23:33.980 --> 00:23:36.280
or get a master in lunacy to sign an order.

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:40.280
Later. After we've got a few things settled.

00:23:40.280 --> 00:23:44.580
From a medical point of view, a plunge into the working world won't do the Earl any harm.

00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:47.630
Won't do him any harm? What about the rest of us?

00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:53.460
He's not dangerous. Besides, I shall be on hand. It'll be an interesting experiment.

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:56.260
A harsh dose of reality can help towards a cure.

00:23:56.260 --> 00:23:59.510
Cure? You've had him here for seven years. Look at him.

00:24:00.220 --> 00:24:30.000
you been doing? Exercising patience and understanding. Something he'll need from his family. Yes, but why haven't you used a knife? Because lobotomy is irrelevant and dangerous in this case. He can't forget being rejected by his mother and father at the age of 11. They sent him away, alone, into a primitive community of licensed bullies and terrorists. You mean he went to public school?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:37.290
Exactly. I'm aware of psychotherapy's messy inadequacies, but I hope that my current research

00:24:37.290 --> 00:24:43.530
will put it all on a more scientific basis. But it depends on my getting a Guldenheim

00:24:43.530 --> 00:24:46.840
grant. Well, never mind about that. What about Jack?

00:24:46.840 --> 00:24:52.050
Remember, he's suffering from delusions of grandeur. In reality, he's an earl, an English

00:24:52.050 --> 00:24:56.660
aristocrat, a member of the ruling class. Naturally, he's come to believe there's only

00:24:56.660 --> 00:25:00.000
one person grander than that, the Lord God Almighty himself.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:01.900
Are you English?

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:03.110
No.

00:25:03.110 --> 00:25:04.510
Ah.

00:25:04.510 --> 00:25:10.360
What's all this, then?

00:25:10.360 --> 00:25:14.360
It is Lordship's effects. Sign here, please.

00:25:14.360 --> 00:25:18.640
Christ!

00:25:18.640 --> 00:25:23.810
If I saw a man eating grass, I'd say he was hungry.

00:25:23.810 --> 00:25:24.990
They'd have him certified.

00:25:24.990 --> 00:25:30.000
They claim that snow is only precipitation and not candid dew.

00:25:30.760 --> 00:25:33.080
