00:42:37.530 --> 00:42:38.970
Because it's his real name.

00:42:39.560 --> 00:42:41.180
Naturally, he rejects it violently.

00:42:42.730 --> 00:42:44.690
If ever he answers to the name of Jack,

00:42:45.360 --> 00:42:47.520
then you know he's on the road to sanity.

00:42:54.070 --> 00:42:59.320
Questions revealing.

00:43:00.060 --> 00:43:02.340
The first one, you asked me, was about love.

00:43:02.340 --> 00:43:14.380
Dr. Herder, he's been with the family for 40 years.

00:43:14.380 --> 00:43:16.650
Man and snivelling boys.

00:43:16.650 --> 00:43:19.080
How do you find the new Earl, Tucker?

00:43:19.080 --> 00:43:20.680
By sniffing.

00:43:20.680 --> 00:43:22.880
He's a gurney.

00:43:22.880 --> 00:43:24.580
A real gurney.

00:43:24.580 --> 00:43:27.200
You don't find him odd?

00:43:27.200 --> 00:43:28.290
Odd?

00:43:30.440 --> 00:43:32.060
So does her.

00:43:32.060 --> 00:43:33.210
Yes.

00:43:33.210 --> 00:43:34.210
Yes.

00:43:34.210 --> 00:43:35.710
Odd.

00:43:35.710 --> 00:43:37.040
Peculiar.

00:43:37.040 --> 00:43:38.340
Oh!

00:43:38.340 --> 00:43:39.550
You mean nutty.

00:43:39.550 --> 00:43:40.550
Yes, he's a nutcase.

00:43:40.550 --> 00:43:44.760
Most of these title fleabags are.

00:43:44.760 --> 00:43:47.760
Rich knobs and privileged arseholes can afford to be bonkers.

00:43:47.760 --> 00:43:50.950
They're living in a dream world, aren't they, sir?

00:43:50.950 --> 00:43:51.950
Life's made too easy for them.

00:43:51.950 --> 00:43:57.080
They don't have to earn a living, so they do just what they want to.

00:43:57.080 --> 00:44:00.000
We'd all look pretty crackers if we went about doing just what we wanted to, wouldn't we?

00:44:02.880 --> 00:44:06.690
Yes. Yes, I suppose, uh...

00:44:06.690 --> 00:44:10.140
The lady left Tucker 30,000 pounds.

00:44:10.140 --> 00:44:13.000
Since then, he's been very outspoken.

00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:17.390
- Lady? - No, thank you.

00:44:17.390 --> 00:44:23.110
Waste not, want not.

00:44:23.110 --> 00:44:27.270
Mind having a look at my back, Doctor?

00:44:27.270 --> 00:44:29.860
Lumbago acting up again.

00:44:32.170 --> 00:44:42.040
the opera by Verdi. It's all the same woman. Marguerite Gauthier, a figure of romance.

00:44:42.040 --> 00:44:47.040
My dear chap, you'll prove my point ipso facto, a divine figure of romance.

00:44:47.040 --> 00:44:53.910
Yeah. Oh, what a pleasant surprise. How are you? In the middle of a debate on the existence

00:44:53.910 --> 00:45:00.000
of my wife, Marguerite. Pray continue, Dinsdale Gurney. I give up. You did say the beginning.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.000
It would be impossible to convince him, Doctor.

00:45:02.020 --> 00:45:03.460
Do you see, it's a play.

00:45:03.460 --> 00:45:06.350
The Lady of the Camellias, it's fiction.

00:45:06.370 --> 00:45:10.050
Yes, a biography of my Marguerite, affectionately known as La Dame of Camellia.

00:45:10.070 --> 00:45:12.410
But you aren't married. The woman doesn't exist.

00:45:12.430 --> 00:45:17.090
Oh, come on. You'll be saying I'm not God, Christ and the Holy Ghost next.

00:45:17.110 --> 00:45:19.710
Well, you're not. I mean, God wouldn't be so ridiculous,

00:45:19.730 --> 00:45:24.200
waving his arms around like a maniac, dressed in a white suit and a red carnation.

00:45:24.200 --> 00:45:29.160
The prophet Ezekiel lay 300 days on his left side and 40 days on his right.

00:45:30.540 --> 00:45:33.980
cut his hair and divided it in three parts. The first part he burnt, the second he chopped

00:45:33.980 --> 00:45:39.440
into pieces, the third he scattered to the wind. It's all a sign of something more important.

00:45:39.440 --> 00:45:42.520
Right, if you're God, reveal your Godhead.

00:45:42.520 --> 00:45:47.280
No, no, no, no. A miracle. Show us a miracle.

00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:49.190
Here's a miracle.

00:45:49.190 --> 00:45:49.690
Why?

00:45:49.690 --> 00:45:51.440
This hand.

00:45:51.440 --> 00:45:58.730
The city network of tissues, nerves, muscles, ligaments, carpels and metacarpals, phalanges,

00:45:58.730 --> 00:46:00.000
and what about the hairy noses?

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:04.660
Wombat. I don't mean that sort of miracle. I mean a proper miracle like the loaves and

00:46:04.660 --> 00:46:12.180
the fishes. Oh, those. You see, ten billion, million miracles a day. Yet you want your

00:46:12.180 --> 00:46:17.340
conjuring tricks, your pretty flimflams. Well, I can't raise Lazarus again. He's decomposed.

00:46:17.420 --> 00:46:29.760
So bring me that table. What are you going to do? Grade one. Galilee miracle. Now.

00:46:30.920 --> 00:46:40.880
instead of raising lazarus i'll raise you a table table ten feet not with the aid of mirrors or

00:46:40.880 --> 00:46:47.950
crippled midgets behind black curtains but by the power of love just love it moves mountains and makes

00:46:47.950 --> 00:47:00.000
the puny weeds split the rock believe in me and loving you

00:47:00.030 --> 00:47:29.890
goodness raise yourself up rise up slowly slowly rise up one foot two three four

00:47:31.150 --> 00:47:33.130
Slowly...

00:47:33.130 --> 00:47:40.610
Slowly...

00:47:40.610 --> 00:47:41.980
Eight...

00:47:41.980 --> 00:47:43.570
Nine...

00:47:43.570 --> 00:47:51.500
Ten...

00:47:51.500 --> 00:47:52.490
Bloody miracle!

00:47:52.490 --> 00:47:53.490
Broken light!

00:47:53.490 --> 00:47:55.490
It didn't rise, there it is!

00:47:55.490 --> 00:47:57.310
B*ckasaur?

00:47:57.310 --> 00:47:58.640
Bleed!

00:47:58.640 --> 00:47:59.650
Did you see it, Doctor?

00:48:00.160 --> 00:48:03.450
- No. - Into my galvanized pressure cooker.

00:48:03.530 --> 00:48:06.530
There's no miracle. There's no wife. She doesn't exist.

00:48:06.610 --> 00:48:08.930
She's fiction, part of a play, part of an opera.

00:48:09.010 --> 00:48:11.400
She's not flesh and blood. She's not real.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:10.310
#

00:50:10.750 --> 00:50:12.750
You should be very grateful to Miss Shelly.

00:50:12.750 --> 00:50:13.750
Grace Shelly is your mistress.

00:50:13.750 --> 00:50:15.750
Miss Shelly's just a hard-working girl.

00:50:15.750 --> 00:50:16.750
On her back!

00:50:16.750 --> 00:50:21.080
First, you try and palm her off on your own brother.

00:50:21.080 --> 00:50:21.910
Ralph needed a wife.

00:50:21.910 --> 00:50:24.060
He took a fancy to young Miss Shelly.

00:50:24.060 --> 00:50:24.980
Well, that didn't work.

00:50:24.980 --> 00:50:26.980
So you tried her for the son.

00:50:26.980 --> 00:50:27.940
It's incestuous.

00:50:27.940 --> 00:50:30.000
Don't talk about it!

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:32.180
Incest, madam, I remember you're Jeremy Gore.

00:50:32.420 --> 00:50:35.560
You went to school with the father, but you went ahead and seduced the son.

00:50:36.050 --> 00:50:37.470
That is incest, madam.

00:50:37.750 --> 00:50:37.970
Oh.

00:50:40.010 --> 00:50:41.910
Well, why the hell didn't you warn us?

00:50:42.010 --> 00:50:42.570
No time.

00:50:43.140 --> 00:50:46.580
After what that trick cyclist told me, I knew he'd never convinced Jackie wasn't married

00:50:46.580 --> 00:50:48.220
and the marguerite didn't exist.

00:50:48.900 --> 00:50:50.760
So I telephoned Grace and explained the position.

00:50:50.940 --> 00:50:53.760
She got hold of some theatrical donks and came down here.

00:50:54.300 --> 00:50:56.200
She put up a first-rate show, I thought.

00:50:56.850 --> 00:50:57.840
Well, it had impact.

00:50:58.700 --> 00:51:00.000
Anyway, Jack believed.

00:51:00.090 --> 00:51:04.310
she was Marguerite. All she has to do now is to convince him he has to marry her again.

00:51:04.310 --> 00:51:11.710
- Dr. Herder is furious. - Furious? He's got no right to be furious. He's not family.

00:51:11.710 --> 00:51:15.870
He could make things difficult by having Jack declared insane before he's produced an heir for you.

00:51:15.870 --> 00:51:22.440
Damn crud! You'll have to keep your eye on him, my dear. I'm gonna have my hands full getting Grace married and pregnant.

00:51:22.440 --> 00:51:30.000
What an entrance! Beautiful, but beautiful! The looks of faces. I should have stuck to the classics.

00:51:30.890 --> 00:51:36.440
Oh, stress is tight. I feel constipated.

00:51:36.440 --> 00:51:38.440
Your flower's wilting, dear.

00:51:38.440 --> 00:51:40.980
Can't be. It's wax.

00:51:40.980 --> 00:51:43.870
Careful your husband-to-be doesn't eat it for breakfast.

00:51:43.870 --> 00:51:51.710
You're right, Charlie boy. She is an ice-cold biddy.

00:51:51.710 --> 00:51:53.710
Oh, she's too clever my half, that woman.

00:51:53.710 --> 00:51:57.100
But I get things done my way. She doesn't know what she wants.

00:51:57.100 --> 00:51:59.860
Oh, but I do, Charlie boy.

00:52:00.890 --> 00:52:06.640
Lady Grace, Lady Grace Gurney, the Countess of Gurney.

00:52:06.640 --> 00:52:08.640
Now, look here, Grace, you mustn't call me Charlie Boy.

00:52:08.640 --> 00:52:09.880
You've got to be careful.

00:52:09.880 --> 00:52:11.060
If that's what you want.

00:52:11.060 --> 00:52:14.070
Oh, it's not what I want, it's what it has to be.

00:52:14.070 --> 00:52:15.910
Oh, I'm very fond of you, my dear.

00:52:15.910 --> 00:52:18.770
