01:01:47.110 --> 01:01:52.560
It's only a nominal £130,000 for the study of paranoid schizophrenic rats.

01:01:52.560 --> 01:01:57.160
Charles, need we be so hasty?

01:01:57.160 --> 01:02:00.000
Charles, God, in his infinite mercy, has seen failure.

01:02:00.060 --> 01:02:05.340
to cloud our nephew's senses, but he will recover, he will recover, Charles. God is merciful.

01:02:05.340 --> 01:02:10.950
Oh yes, you must believe that, Charles. God is merciful in spite of all appearances.

01:02:10.950 --> 01:02:16.910
We cannot wait upon God's mercy, Bertie. Everything is going to part. Dr. Herder agrees.

01:02:16.910 --> 01:02:30.000
Herder? Herder. Is he English? No. We insert fine silver wires into the rat's

01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:37.970
That rat's behavior is then controlled by the strength of the current passing through them.

01:02:37.970 --> 01:02:44.620
By pressing a button and stimulating one area of the midbrain, the rat is made to feel threatened.

01:02:44.620 --> 01:02:46.760
It attacks any rat inside.

01:02:46.760 --> 01:02:51.470
There's really no threat, but the midbrain can't tell the difference.

01:02:51.470 --> 01:02:54.670
Roughly the same thing happens with human paranoids.

01:02:54.670 --> 01:02:59.860
But an unknown area of the brain is stimulated and they feel threatened without cause.

01:03:00.860 --> 01:03:03.360
Naturally, men aren't rats.

01:03:03.360 --> 01:03:09.550
Only a man would say so.

01:03:09.550 --> 01:03:15.080
Our next step is to conduct similar experiments on the human brain.

01:03:15.080 --> 01:03:19.230
You see, today rats, tomorrow the world.

01:03:19.230 --> 01:03:22.020
Where will you wire for visions?

01:03:22.020 --> 01:03:24.790
First of all, myself, naturally.

01:03:24.790 --> 01:03:29.190
You see, and if I press a button, you'll feel fear.

01:03:30.600 --> 01:03:31.640
Love?

01:03:31.640 --> 01:03:32.880
Love?

01:03:32.880 --> 01:03:34.670
No.

01:03:34.670 --> 01:03:38.290
Desire?

01:03:38.290 --> 01:03:39.970
What?

01:03:39.970 --> 01:03:42.460
By pressing a little button?

01:03:42.460 --> 01:03:46.830
Oh, think of the risk, Doctor.

01:03:46.830 --> 01:03:50.680
There is only one commandment a doctor need ever worry about.

01:03:50.680 --> 01:03:54.890
Love shall not advertise.

01:04:31.050 --> 01:04:35.540
My heart rises with the sun.

01:04:35.540 --> 01:04:44.410
I am purged of doubts and negative innuendos.

01:04:44.410 --> 01:04:47.420
Today I want to bless everything.

01:04:47.420 --> 01:04:52.490
Bless the crawfish with its scuttling walk.

01:04:52.490 --> 01:04:56.260
Bless the trout, pilchard and periwinkle.

01:04:56.260 --> 01:05:00.000
Bless Ted Smoothie of Periwinkle.

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.180
22 East Hackney Road.

01:05:03.470 --> 01:05:04.830
Bless the mealy red pole,

01:05:05.110 --> 01:05:06.550
the black-gloved wallaby

01:05:06.550 --> 01:05:08.910
and W.C. Fields who's dead

01:05:08.910 --> 01:05:09.790
but lives on.

01:05:10.910 --> 01:05:12.890
Bless the snotty-nosed giraffe.

01:05:14.000 --> 01:05:14.900
Bless the buffalo.

01:05:16.130 --> 01:05:18.610
Bless the society of women engineers.

01:05:20.670 --> 01:05:21.710
Pygmy hippos.

01:05:22.620 --> 01:05:23.590
Bless the mighty

01:06:15.740 --> 01:06:30.000
we are gathered here together in any sight of God

01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:37.380
in the face of this company to join together this man and this woman in holy matrimony which is

01:06:37.380 --> 01:06:46.470
an honourable estate in... Instituted by me in the time of man's innocence. Get off, Bertie. Therefore,

01:06:46.470 --> 01:06:55.780
if there be any in this company who can show just cause why these two may not be joined together,

01:06:55.780 --> 01:07:00.000
let him speak now or forever hold his hand.

01:07:04.760 --> 01:07:05.900
and half dead helots.

01:07:06.100 --> 01:07:07.780
Quiet man, show some respect.

01:07:08.300 --> 01:07:09.860
I always show respect, sir.

01:07:11.040 --> 01:07:12.200
That's what I'm paid for.

01:07:13.230 --> 01:07:16.030
No one can say I don't show respect.

01:07:21.930 --> 01:07:23.700
And charge.

01:07:24.740 --> 01:07:27.340
Require and charge you both

01:07:27.340 --> 01:07:30.000
that if either of you know of any impediment

01:07:30.250 --> 01:07:34.430
while ye may not lawfully be joined together,

01:07:34.490 --> 01:07:38.630
that you dee now... you dee...

01:07:39.100 --> 01:07:42.320
ye do now confess it.

01:07:42.380 --> 01:07:45.010
Yes, I'm afraid I do know an impediment.

01:07:45.060 --> 01:07:48.470
But it's only a rhetorical question, like all the others in the wedding service.

01:07:48.550 --> 01:07:50.790
Oh, 'tis no good glossing o'er the facts.

01:07:50.930 --> 01:07:55.660
Certain Roman Catholic knackers think I'm already married to the Virgin Mary.

01:07:55.800 --> 01:07:58.100
We're not concerned with what other people think,

01:07:58.150 --> 01:07:59.800
especially Roman Catholics.

01:08:00.670 --> 01:08:02.720
Get on with it, Bertie, come on now.

01:08:02.720 --> 01:08:06.700
Will thou, will thou take this woman to thy wedded wife

01:08:06.700 --> 01:08:10.700
to live together in a holy wedlock under God's ordinance?

01:08:10.700 --> 01:08:12.700
Will, will, will thou love her?

01:08:12.700 --> 01:08:15.700
From the bottom of my soul to the tip of my penis,

01:08:15.700 --> 01:08:18.700
like the sun in its brightness, the moon in its glory,

01:08:18.700 --> 01:08:21.700
no breeze stirs that doesn't bear my love.

01:08:24.220 --> 01:08:28.930
Come on, Bertie, come on.

01:08:28.930 --> 01:08:30.000
Just bless you.

01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:34.530
- But will you love me? - I will.

01:08:34.530 --> 01:08:39.590
- Will thou take this man to their wedding... - I will.

01:08:39.590 --> 01:08:43.400
- To live together in holy... - I will.

01:08:43.400 --> 01:08:47.500
- Who giveth this woman? - I do.

01:08:47.500 --> 01:08:53.650
- Get him, Father. - Repeat after me.

01:08:53.650 --> 01:09:00.000
I, Jesse, take thee, gracefully.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.060
Shelly, to my wedded wife.

01:09:02.500 --> 01:09:05.860
I, J.C., the holy flying roller, the morning star,

01:09:06.020 --> 01:09:08.020
take thee, Marguerite, called Grace Shelly,

01:09:08.100 --> 01:09:10.240
because she doesn't speak French to my wedded wife.

01:09:12.760 --> 01:09:13.520
Where are you going, Bertie?

01:09:15.140 --> 01:09:19.030
Repeat after me.

01:09:19.250 --> 01:09:20.070
Oh, I know the lines.

01:09:20.790 --> 01:09:23.350
I, Grace Shelly, take thee, J.C., to my wedded husband.

01:09:23.510 --> 01:09:24.770
Better, worse, richer, poorer.

01:09:24.890 --> 01:09:27.250
This day, sickness, health, I plight thee, my troth.

01:09:28.650 --> 01:09:29.290
Thee, my troth.

01:09:29.290 --> 01:09:29.510
Yes.

01:09:30.440 --> 01:09:34.640
Well, then, as much as you are now bound in holy wedlock,

01:09:34.640 --> 01:09:38.840
I now pronounce thee man and wife.

01:09:38.840 --> 01:09:41.330
God, join together.

01:09:41.330 --> 01:09:43.830
No man, no man put asunder.

01:09:43.830 --> 01:09:48.330
In the name of the Father, the Son, and the Holy, the Holy.

01:09:48.330 --> 01:09:52.180
Lord, have mercy on me.

01:10:27.770 --> 01:10:30.000
No guests, no reception.

01:10:30.000 --> 01:10:34.000
two plates of curled up sandwiches and a deformed wedding cake.

01:10:34.000 --> 01:10:36.000
Well, it's not my fault, your ladyship.

01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:39.840
Ladyship? That's better.

01:10:39.840 --> 01:10:41.870
I'll watch them creep and crawl at Harrods.

01:10:41.870 --> 01:10:44.820
We thought you'd like a nice quiet affair.

01:10:44.820 --> 01:10:45.670
Ha! Quiet's right!

01:10:45.670 --> 01:10:48.750
And what about a toast to the newlyweds or something, you know?

01:10:48.750 --> 01:10:53.500
Oh, very well. Here's to long life and happiness...

01:10:53.500 --> 01:10:55.480
...to the bride and groom.

01:10:55.480 --> 01:10:56.480
To the bride and groom.

01:10:56.480 --> 01:10:59.410
Thank you. In reply, I name this ship...

01:11:00.000 --> 01:11:15.030
loving kindness may I keep her on all who say that I you should have seen the late Earl's

01:11:15.030 --> 01:11:24.680
wedding my lady 500 guests the creamed menthe wastrel and all may their carbonized bones

01:11:24.680 --> 01:11:30.000
rot in hell shut up can't say that I like the

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:37.200
idea of you being alone with him. You're a beauty. Everything's yours, even if you've

01:11:37.200 --> 01:11:46.480
given it away. One minute's silence, please. What for? For all the dead books of World

01:11:46.480 --> 01:11:57.730
War I. For Mr. Moto, Cisco Kid, and me. Muffle the drums. Silence. Shhh.

01:12:18.650 --> 01:12:19.550
Terrible, isn't it?

01:12:20.110 --> 01:12:22.820
That's why I sing, dance, talk.

01:12:24.570 --> 01:12:25.190
And love.

01:12:28.600 --> 01:12:30.000
Oh, really?

01:12:30.730 --> 01:12:38.100
Charleston we sang, and village bells rang, and the beautiful night we were married.

01:12:38.100 --> 01:12:47.490
All the roses they bloom for the bride and groom, for the beautiful night we were married.

01:12:47.490 --> 01:12:51.220
Tuck on! Tuck on!

01:12:51.220 --> 01:12:59.380
I thought you'd like me to liven up this week. Where'd they go?

01:13:00.160 --> 01:13:05.860
of course. Must say, wouldn't I have to be in her shoes tonight? It's not her shoes he'll

01:13:05.860 --> 01:13:30.000
be in, Master Dinnersdale. Any good performer does. You have to be keyed up to

01:13:30.000 --> 01:13:39.760
give a good show. I've done it all. From Stanislavski to strip. Greasy makeup towels, cracked

01:13:39.760 --> 01:13:47.120
mirrors, rhinestones and beads. What a world. Us anglers can't be loved. Funny. Do the same

01:13:47.120 --> 01:13:54.650
act later at the Begal for twice the money without removing a stitch. Of course, some

01:13:54.650 --> 01:13:57.190
women can strip without taking their clothes off.

01:14:06.270 --> 01:14:11.570
Nobody could call me under sex, but I could never get worked up watching some man strip

01:14:11.570 --> 01:14:13.550
down to suspenders and jockstraps.

01:14:13.550 --> 01:14:25.260
Well, where's the fun?

01:14:25.260 --> 01:14:30.000
Some people just prefer the smell of a steak better to the steak itself.

01:14:30.920 --> 01:14:39.280
could see me now. It's what she always wanted for me. The big time. She found it hard to settle down

01:14:39.280 --> 01:14:52.810
to civilian life after being in the touring company of Choo Chin Chow. You worry about me

01:14:52.810 --> 01:14:58.210
fitting in. All I have to do is play it cool.

01:15:05.180 --> 01:15:07.360
I can cock my little finger with the bat.

01:15:12.560 --> 01:15:19.260
Darling, darling, I'm waiting.

01:15:25.180 --> 01:15:26.880
Ridiculous, it's not dignified.

01:15:27.220 --> 01:15:29.010
Dignity has nothing to do with divinity.

01:15:29.290 --> 01:15:30.000
Oh, look, I'm not.

01:15:30.000 --> 01:15:32.540
I hear, not now, a bike! You're mad.

01:15:32.540 --> 01:15:33.720
Don't be frightened.

01:15:33.720 --> 01:15:35.200
I'm not frightened.

01:15:35.200 --> 01:15:37.040
I just didn't expect to see my husband

01:15:37.040 --> 01:15:39.040
riding a three-wheel bike on his wedding night.

01:15:39.040 --> 01:15:40.340
It's the only way to travel.

01:15:40.340 --> 01:15:55.850
Remember, God loves you, God wants you, God needs you.

01:17:05.080 --> 01:17:11.780
What did he do?

01:17:11.780 --> 01:17:14.440
Rode around on a three-wheel bike.

01:17:14.440 --> 01:17:16.130
Filthy beast.

01:17:16.130 --> 01:17:19.910
Joseph must have been one of the governor's old bikes.

01:17:19.910 --> 01:17:22.210
The attic's full of his junk.

01:17:22.210 --> 01:17:27.080
So, he just rode about all night then.

01:17:27.080 --> 01:17:29.220
First the bike, then me.

01:17:32.330 --> 01:17:36.210
His mind may be wonky, but there's certainly nothing wrong with the rest of his anatomy.

01:17:37.160 --> 01:17:39.160
The girl is undamnably virile.

01:17:40.170 --> 01:17:42.490
I thought you'd be delighted to find out he's not impotent.

01:17:43.230 --> 01:17:46.650
Why? Delighted.

01:17:47.360 --> 01:17:48.490
Good morning.

01:17:50.210 --> 01:17:51.610
Well, was it successful?

01:17:52.250 --> 01:17:53.580
Should have sold bleeding tickets.

01:17:54.090 --> 01:17:55.790
Really, Claire? How could you ask that?

01:17:56.110 --> 01:17:57.460
It was your idea, remember?

01:17:58.090 --> 01:18:00.000
Found if he was incapable, somebody else would.

01:18:00.440 --> 01:18:07.020
to step into the bridge for? Charles, tell her to keep her sharp tongue and blown mind

